{"nodes": [{"id": "plans_03a_ui_build_runbook_procedure", "label": "Phase 3a UI Build Runbook", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md", "source_location": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md:1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The procedure to 03a's policy: the per-screen loop, measurement rules, the verify setup, kit discipline, the identity seam, and the traps that have already cost time."}, {"id": "plans_03a_ui_build_runbook_per_screen_loop", "label": "Per-Screen Build Loop", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md", "source_location": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md:32", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Build one screen, screenshot it live, diff it, show the owner, wait for confirm. It was overridden by the owner for frames 02-06, which measurably cost accuracy versus the dashboard's per-screen loop. Concession that works: build the first screen of a new role alone to establish that role's geometry family, then batch within the role."}, {"id": "plans_03a_ui_build_runbook_2x_frame_rule", "label": "Exports Are 2x of 1440x810 - Halve Everything", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md", "source_location": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md:42", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Halving lands the QAC wordmark on exactly 20px, nav labels 15, stat numerals 20, LEVEL n 12 and the top bar 59 - which is what settled the question."}, {"id": "plans_03a_ui_build_runbook_playwright_verify", "label": "Playwright Verify Setup", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md", "source_location": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md:57", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Viewport 1440x810 with deviceScaleFactor 2 gives a 2880x1620 PNG identical in size to the export, so landmarks compare as raw integers. Never measure a portal screen wider than 1440 - the shell zooms above that and every landmark will be wrong."}, {"id": "plans_03a_ui_build_runbook_pixel_diff_floor", "label": "The 2.8% Antialiasing Pixel-Diff Floor", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md", "source_location": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md:74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Resize both to 2880x1620 and count pixels differing >30/255. ~2.8% is the antialiasing-only floor; 4% is fine; 9%+ means something structural, or artwork that differs from what the designer used."}, {"id": "plans_03a_ui_build_runbook_content_padding_families", "label": "Content Padding Differs Per Screen Family", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md", "source_location": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md:55", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Dashboard/assignment/events/reports 57px, document browser 74px, profile 81px. Measure it per family; do not assume."}, {"id": "plans_03a_ui_build_runbook_identity_seam", "label": "The Identity Seam", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md", "source_location": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md:100", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The signed-in user is a hardcoded constant, so no other role is reachable without editing source. Replace it with getCurrentUser() reading a dev cookie into PORTAL_USERS. The cookie holds a user key, not a role, because the top bar shows name, position and avatar - switching role alone would leave one person's name on every role. Later this becomes supabase.auth.getUser() + app_metadata.role: one function body changes."}, {"id": "plans_03a_ui_build_runbook_sidebar_must_receive_user", "label": "The Sidebar Must Receive the User", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md", "source_location": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md:115", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "PortalTopBar and PortalSidebar both import the hardcoded constant directly today. The sidebar is a client component because it needs usePathname, so it has to receive the user as a prop rather than call the server-only accessor."}, {"id": "plans_03a_ui_build_runbook_empty_sidebar_by_design", "label": "An Empty Sidebar Is by Design, Say So", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md", "source_location": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md:122", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "PORTAL_NAV only defines qac_personnel. Until a role's frames land its sidebar is empty by design - say so in the switcher rather than rendering a blank rail, or it reads as a bug."}, {"id": "plans_03a_ui_build_runbook_kit_discipline", "label": "Kit Discipline", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md", "source_location": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md:80", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Read kit/index.ts before building any screen. Reuse what is there, extend with a prop rather than forking a near-duplicate, and the moment a second screen needs something a page has inline, move it to the kit and update the first screen."}, {"id": "plans_03a_ui_build_runbook_formatting_in_components", "label": "Keep Formatting in Components, Not Fake Data", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md", "source_location": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md:94", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stat.note is currently a finished sentence ('1.10% Since last month'); it should take deltaPct and compose in StatCard. This is what makes the eventual real-data swap a data change instead of a rewrite."}, {"id": "plans_03a_ui_build_runbook_fake_data_swap_point", "label": "data.ts Is the Single Backend Swap Point", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md", "source_location": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md:99", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "plans_03a_ui_build_runbook_missing_routes_404", "label": "/portal/performance and /portal/feedback 404", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md", "source_location": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md:29", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Already linked from the sidebar but have no frame. Do not invent them."}, {"id": "plans_03a_ui_build_runbook_build_order", "label": "Build Order: login, register, _shared, seam, roles", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md", "source_location": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md:129", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Login and register are built together because they share layout, background and form controls - doing them together is what puts those in the kit once instead of twice."}, {"id": "plans_03a_ui_build_runbook_register_per_role", "label": "Register Has One Subfolder Per Role", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md", "source_location": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md:132", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Build one role's registration screen fully, extract its form chrome to the kit, then do the other three. The four almost certainly differ only in which fields they ask for; building all four inline leaves four copies of the same form to reconcile."}, {"id": "plans_03a_ui_build_runbook_registration_entitlement_question", "label": "How Does a Registrant Prove Role Entitlement?", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md", "source_location": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md:216", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Four separate sign-up forms means something has to stop a stranger opening the qac_admin one. Admin invite links, a domain-restricted email, or a pending-approval state are the usual answers - and it is a UI-visible decision, so ask before building the forms. The role must never be settable by the user at signup."}, {"id": "plans_03a_ui_build_runbook_register_url_shape_question", "label": "What URL Shape Do the Registration Screens Take?", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md", "source_location": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md:225", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "/register/[role], four literal paths, or one /register with a role step - affects routing before any screen is built."}, {"id": "plans_03a_ui_build_runbook_schema_questions", "label": "Schema-Shaped Questions to Ask as You Go", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md", "source_location": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md:211", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "They cost nothing now and a UI assumption that contradicts the real model is a rebuild, not a rewire: dual roles, one accreditation per program or many cycles, rep scoping, and whether accreditors see only assigned accreditations."}, {"id": "plans_03a_ui_build_runbook_role_checklist", "label": "Per-Role Frame/Build Checklist", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md", "source_location": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md:155", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "qac_personnel is 12 frames exported and 12 screens built, owner confirmation still open; login, register (five rows), _shared, program_representative, internal_accreditor and qac_admin are all unticked."}, {"id": "plans_03a_ui_build_runbook_portal_bold_rule", "label": "Portal Bold Is font-semibold", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md", "source_location": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md:191", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Except stat numerals and the Poppins wordmark, which are 700."}], "edges": [{"source": "plans_03a_ui_build_runbook_procedure", "target": "plans_03a_ui_build_runbook_per_screen_loop", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md", "source_location": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md:1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plans_03a_ui_build_runbook_procedure", "target": "plans_03a_ui_build_runbook_2x_frame_rule", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md", "source_location": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md:1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plans_03a_ui_build_runbook_procedure", "target": "plans_03a_ui_build_runbook_playwright_verify", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md", "source_location": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md:1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plans_03a_ui_build_runbook_procedure", "target": "plans_03a_ui_build_runbook_pixel_diff_floor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md", "source_location": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md:1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "plans_03a_ui_build_runbook_procedure", "target": "plans_03a_ui_build_runbook_content_padding_families", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md", "source_location": "plans/03a-ui-build-runbook.md:1", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "pla